@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Navigating Azure DevOps UI";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <h1 class="text-center text-primary">Navigating Azure DevOps UI</h1>
    <p class="text-center lead">A comprehensive guide to understanding and using the Azure DevOps user interface effectively.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Introduction Section -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">Introduction</h2>
        <p>
            Azure DevOps provides a powerful and intuitive UI to manage the entire DevOps lifecycle. Understanding its navigation and features ensures smooth collaboration and productivity.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-devops-dashboard.jpg" alt="Azure DevOps UI Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure DevOps UI Dashboard</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Main Components of Azure DevOps -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Main Components of Azure DevOps UI</h2>
        <p>
            The Azure DevOps UI consists of various sections that help teams manage projects efficiently.
        </p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Dashboard:</strong> A customizable overview of project status, work items, and analytics.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Repos:</strong> Manage Git repositories for source control.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Pipelines:</strong> Build, test, and deploy applications using CI/CD.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Boards:</strong> Agile project management with Kanban, Scrum, and task tracking.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Artifacts:</strong> Manage and store packages for project dependencies.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Test Plans:</strong> Create and manage test cases and automated testing workflows.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-devops-components.jpg" alt="Azure DevOps Components" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Key sections of Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Navigating the UI -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-info">How to Navigate the Azure DevOps UI</h2>
        <p>
            Navigating the Azure DevOps UI is intuitive. Follow these steps to efficiently access various features:
        </p>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item">Log in to your <a href="https://dev.azure.com" target="_blank">Azure DevOps account</a>.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Select your organization and choose a project from the dashboard.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Use the left-hand navigation panel to access different services like Repos, Pipelines, and Boards.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Use the search bar at the top to find specific work items, repositories, or pipelines.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Customize dashboards to display key project metrics and reports.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-devops-navigation.jpg" alt="Azure DevOps Navigation" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Navigation in Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Tips for Efficient Navigation -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">Tips for Efficient Navigation</h2>
        <p>
            To make the most out of Azure DevOps, follow these best practices:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Pin frequently used projects:</strong> Keep important projects easily accessible.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Use keyboard shortcuts:</strong> Speed up navigation with shortcuts.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Customize dashboards:</strong> Set up widgets and reports for quick insights.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Leverage search functionality:</strong> Quickly find items with the search bar.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Enable notifications:</strong> Stay updated with project changes.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-devops-tips.jpg" alt="Azure DevOps Tips" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Best practices for using Azure DevOps</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-secondary">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Understanding the Azure DevOps UI is key to optimizing workflow efficiency. With intuitive navigation, seamless integration, and customization options, teams can enhance their DevOps experience and project management capabilities.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-devops-success.jpg" alt="Successful Azure DevOps Usage" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Mastering the UI leads to improved DevOps efficiency.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>